course: dictionary
lesson: 8847
title: Shivery: cold, scared, or tingly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shivery is a describing word, an adjective. Its first meaning is simple: you feel cold and shake a little, or you feel as if you might shiver. Read the story around the word for clues. «She wakes up hot and shivery» is about her body, not the weather.
explain: Shivery has a second meaning too. A spooky story can be shivery, which means it gives you a slightly scared, tingly feeling down your back. The word tells you how the story makes you feel, not how cold the room is.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Ask: is this about a body, or about a feeling? If a child is hot and shivery, and then stays in bed, the clues point to being ill, so shivery means feeling cold and shaking. In a ghost story, the clues are about scary things, so shivery means tingly and scared.
fact: Shivery means feeling cold and shaking a little, or feeling as if you might shiver.
fact: Shivery can also mean giving a slightly scared, tingly feeling, like a spooky story.
fact: The word «shivery» comes from shiver, so the two words are related.
fact: «Shivery» can change form: shivery, shiverier, shiveriest, or more shivery.
fact: When you feel hot and shivery, it can be a sign of a fever, so tell an adult.
exercise: «She wakes up hot and shivery.» What does shivery mean here? | Sweating and smiling | Ready for a party | Very tall and thin | *Feeling cold and shaking a little
exercise: Ella says a «shivery ghost story» is a story about a sunny beach. What does shivery mean in this phrase? | Very loud noises | A hungry feeling | A bored, yawning feeling | *A slightly scared, tingly feeling
exercise: «She wakes up hot and shivery; she tells her mum.» Why might she tell her mum? | *Feeling hot and shivery can be a sign of a fever, so an adult should know | Because shivery means she wants a new toy | Because she is bored of school | To ask for a party
test: «Hot and shivery, she stays in bed with a drink of water.» What does shivery mean? | Very wet and sticky | Happy and full of energy | A tall, shivering tree | *Feeling cold and shaking, as if she might shiver
test: Grandpa reads a shivery tale, and Max pulls his blanket up. What does shivery suggest about the tale? | Boring and very long | *It gives a slightly scared, tingly feeling | It is written in a foreign language | It is about a sunny picnic
exam: «She is back at school after her fever has been gone for a day.» Jayden says shivery means the same as tired. Which is the best answer? | No, shivery means very fast | Yes, but only at bedtime | Yes, shivery and tired mean exactly the same thing | *No, shivery is about feeling cold and shaking, or a tingly scared feeling, not tiredness
